+# Agents design a named piece of work
+
+**Outcome:** The product owner names a piece of work. Agents shape it into a slice that one person can test, make its plan and write its eval. The product owner confirms each part as it is made.
+
+**Why:** Today the product owner must guide each step of the design by hand. No play designs the work for Garura's own work: the product owner found this while #760 started. When agents do the design, the work is faster and it stays inside its design.
+
+**Asked by:** the product owner
+
+**Proof it is met:**
+- A business intent goes from its issue to an approved design.
+- The design has a slice that one person can test end to end on one surface, with the features it needs in build order.
+- The design has a plan that a person can run and track: the plan file, one epic for the slice, and one story for each feature.
+- The design has an eval that tests, from the outside, if the business intent is met.
+- Each of the three plays ends at one confirmation by the product owner.
+- A play runs each step. No step is done by hand.
+- No builder is given the eval, and a check flags each build session that read the evals folder.
+
+**Must not:** Do not send the slice, the plan or the eval to the tracker before the product owner confirms it, and do not start a build before that. Do not let a builder read the eval. Do not shape an ICE that is not ready. Do not ask the person a question that the model or memory answers. Do not include the design, build, test or validation of an epic (#819), the release plays or /learn-outcomes, or the upgrade of an older product model (#835).
+
+Written by /shape-slice from issue #788 on 2026-10-24, because the product model had no page for it. The product owner confirmed it on 2026-10-24 (#844).
+
+**Stage:** confirmed — by the product owner, 2026-10-24
+**Tracker:** #788
